WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:01.710
Instructor: Hey everyone, welcome back.

00:01.710 --> 00:03.630
So as I've been working on this course,

00:03.630 --> 00:06.120
I've referred to this section internally,

00:06.120 --> 00:07.410
it's just me but,

00:07.410 --> 00:10.400
in my head internally as GitHub odds and ends.

00:10.400 --> 00:12.990
I don't really think that's a fair title.

00:12.990 --> 00:15.120
There are some very important pieces in here

00:15.120 --> 00:17.640
and then some odds and ends.

00:17.640 --> 00:20.040
It's just another one of those motley sections

00:20.040 --> 00:23.640
and assortments of topics that have to do with GitHub.

00:23.640 --> 00:25.189
So the first thing we covered

00:25.189 --> 00:27.720
is the difference between having a public and private repo

00:27.720 --> 00:29.040
and what it means.

00:29.040 --> 00:31.980
That's gonna be critical but also very easy.

00:31.980 --> 00:34.650
Then we talked about adding collaborators to repos.

00:34.650 --> 00:36.900
How do we add somebody else and give them permission

00:36.900 --> 00:39.881
to push for example to a project?

00:39.881 --> 00:42.390
That's going to be critical as well.

00:42.390 --> 00:43.470
You do that all the time,

00:43.470 --> 00:45.540
assuming you collaborate.

00:45.540 --> 00:47.910
We talked about ReadMe files.

00:47.910 --> 00:49.200
Which is important.

00:49.200 --> 00:50.790
You may have seen this before.

00:50.790 --> 00:52.920
All caps README.md,

00:52.920 --> 00:55.020
stands for Markdown, md.

00:55.020 --> 00:57.780
They play a particular role in GitHub repositories.

00:57.780 --> 01:01.620
Pretty much every repo has one but it's not critical.

01:01.620 --> 01:03.510
Important, sort of best practice,

01:03.510 --> 01:05.760
it's a good habit to get into.

01:05.760 --> 01:07.350
Anyways, I'm getting ahead of myself.

01:07.350 --> 01:09.120
It's important but not critical.

01:09.120 --> 01:11.310
Then I talked about markdown.

01:11.310 --> 01:12.720
If you're not familiar with markdown,

01:12.720 --> 01:14.859
it is not a Git or GitHub topic,

01:14.859 --> 01:18.360
but to make a ReadMe we do write markdown.

01:18.360 --> 01:20.160
So it's related.

01:20.160 --> 01:21.870
If you already know markdown skip that.

01:21.870 --> 01:23.250
If you don't, check it out.

01:23.250 --> 01:25.200
But remember markdown is a thing on its own

01:25.200 --> 01:27.810
and it's not tied to Git and GitHub.

01:27.810 --> 01:30.570
And then two other things I'm gonna say are nice to have,

01:30.570 --> 01:32.610
definitely not important or critical,

01:32.610 --> 01:35.490
a feature on GitHub called gists.

01:35.490 --> 01:36.540
That's all I'll say about it.

01:36.540 --> 01:38.250
They're nice to have but a lot of people

01:38.250 --> 01:39.690
just don't even use them.

01:39.690 --> 01:41.460
And then GitHub Pages,

01:41.460 --> 01:44.490
a very nice to have tool from GitHub that allows us,

01:44.490 --> 01:48.300
it helps us to easily host webpages, static webpages,

01:48.300 --> 01:50.130
from our repositories.

01:50.130 --> 01:53.730
So very nice to have but also not at all critical.

01:53.730 --> 01:55.650
It's just not a feature of Git,

01:55.650 --> 01:57.630
it's a feature of GitHub.

01:57.630 --> 01:59.880
But it's one that's pleasant and it's nice

01:59.880 --> 02:00.960
especially if you're starting out

02:00.960 --> 02:03.150
and you want a personal site, a portfolio site,

02:03.150 --> 02:04.320
you wanna demo a project,

02:04.320 --> 02:05.730
it's very useful.

02:05.730 --> 02:06.990
Anyway, you get it.

02:06.990 --> 02:10.110
We'll talk about it in the actual video on GitHub Pages.

02:10.110 --> 02:12.480
The main things I hope you take away from this section

02:12.480 --> 02:15.210
are really just about settings in a repo.

02:15.210 --> 02:16.620
Public versus private,

02:16.620 --> 02:17.453
permissions,

02:17.453 --> 02:18.450
adding collaborators,

02:18.450 --> 02:20.910
and then some GitHub adjacent topics,

02:20.910 --> 02:22.770
like markdown and ReadMe files.

02:22.770 --> 02:24.840
GitHub pages, worth knowing about,

02:24.840 --> 02:25.740
nice to have,

02:25.740 --> 02:27.240
they're in the course for a reason,

02:27.240 --> 02:28.260
but just not critical.

02:28.260 --> 02:29.093
Okay, I gotta shut up.

02:29.093 --> 02:29.943
Bye.
